    {
      "id": "why-it-matters",
      "title": "Why it matters",
      "body": "These phrases keep the interaction cooperative when repeating the same words is not helping. For \"I don't understand\", the useful move is asking for one clear help action before adding more words. If the first reply is still unclear, move to showing, writing, or pointing.",
      "presentation": "plain-text"
    },
    {
      "id": "traveler-insight",
      "title": "Traveler insight",
      "body": "In When You Don't Understand, locals often answer with a slower repeat, a pointed explanation, or a switch to writing rather than a long explanation. That makes Tôi không hiểu strongest when you say it once, pause, and let the other person show the next step. If speech still does not land, move to writing, pointing, or showing the exact word on your phone.",
